# XSH munmap()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Page sizes come from sysconf(_SC_PAGESIZE); addresses passed are page
# multiples (the implementation may require that). Signals are seen by
# touching memory in a child process.

assertion  XSH.munmap.001
anchor     functions/munmap.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/V2_chap02.html#2.8.3.3
class      required
since      2001
says       After munmap() of the second page of a two-page mapping returns
           0, a load from or a store to that page raises SIGSEGV, and the
           first page can still be loaded.
test       t/001-segv-after.c

assertion  XSH.munmap.002
anchor     functions/munmap.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       munmap(second page, 1) of a three-page mapping removes all of
           the second page (a load from its last byte raises SIGSEGV) and
           neither neighbour.
test       t/002-whole-pages.c

assertion  XSH.munmap.003
anchor     functions/munmap.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/V2_chap02.html#2.3
class      required
since      2001
says       munmap() of a page-aligned page with no mapping, between two
           mapped pages, returns 0 and leaves the neighbours mapped.
note       DESCRIPTION gives the call no effect and no error condition
           applies, so XSH 2.3 makes it succeed.
test       t/003-nothing-mapped.c

assertion  XSH.munmap.004
anchor     functions/munmap.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       After a store to a MAP_PRIVATE mapping of a file and munmap() of
           it, read() of the file and a new mapping of it show the
           original byte.
note       NOTINUSE where MAP_PRIVATE fails with ENOTSUP.
test       t/004-private-discarded.c

assertion  XSH.munmap.005
anchor     functions/munmap.html#ERRORS/EINVAL
class      required
since      2001
says       munmap() of a mapped page with len 0 fails with EINVAL, and the
           page stays mapped.
test       t/005-len-zero.c

assertion  XSH.munmap.006
anchor     functions/munmap.html#ERRORS/EINVAL
class      required
since      2001
says       munmap() of two pages starting at the last page-aligned address
           (the range runs past the top of any address space) fails with
           EINVAL.
test       t/006-outside-einval.c
